<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jorge Tadeo Lozano</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1771">1771</a>–<a href="/years/1816">1816</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jorge Tadeo Lozano was a New Granadan naturalist and politician who became the first president of the Free and Independent State of Cundinamarca in 1811. A member of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bogota">Bogotá</a> elite, he headed a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constitutional-monarchy">constitutional monarchy</a> that still acknowledged Ferdinand VII, but was soon displaced by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antonio-narino">Antonio Nariño</a>. After the Spanish reconquest he was executed by order of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pablo-morillo">Pablo Morillo</a> in 1816.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jorge-tadeo-lozano.jpg" alt="Jorge Tadeo Lozano" width="221" height="300" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Víctor Moscoso · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lozajorg.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
